webmvs patch 0018: incremental checkpoints. On top of 0001-0008, 0011-0015, 0017.
- cckddasd.c/cckd.h: a bitmap per CCKD file of the 4 KB blocks written since the last full checkpoint copy
  (cckd_write, cut part of cckd_ftruncate); cckd_ckpt_dev() copies (full) or writes the marked blocks into one
  delta file (shadows.dlt); helpers for sr.c.
- sr.c: checkpoint <dir> incr=1 base=<full dir> [maxdelta=%] [maxshadow=%] [verify=1]: a delta = the pages of
  main storage whose XXH64 differs from the base (SR_SYS_MSBASE + SR_SYS_MSDELTA in machine.srf) + shadows.dlt;
  full when there is no tracked base or the delta is too large. The read-back crc32 and the fsyncs of the .srf
  and of the delta file run after the CPUs are started again. resume <file> track=1 adopts the resumed
  checkpoint's base. sr_ckpt_progress counts ended checkpoints (lock-free wait in the page's pagehide).
- msgenu.h: HHC02030I gets the kind (full/delta) at the end. sr.h: the two new keys.
QPL 1.0: a modification of SDL Hercules Hyperion, distributed as a separate patch.

